{"parentUuid":"48b178a8-6925-4a5a-9279-d013d934a1ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01K5h1UDu9RZDYtASjFeSM8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have a clear picture. Let me give you the diagnosis.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe `recap` command has a misleading-error bug at **`cmd/entire/cli/recap.go:125-129`**:\n\n```go\nclient, err := NewAuthenticatedAPIClient(f.insecureHTTP)\nif err != nil {\n    fmt.Fprintln(errW, \"Sign in with `entire login` to use `entire recap`.\")\n    return NewSilentError(err)\n}\n```\n\nIt tells users to re-login regardless of *why* the auth client failed. `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient` (`api_client.go:14`) has **three** failure paths:\n\n| Failure | Re-login fixes it? |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Token missing from keyring | ✅ yes |\n| 2. Keyring read error (locked, permissions) | ❌ no |\n| 3. Base URL is `http://` and `--insecure-http-auth` not passed | ❌ no — token is already valid |\n\nThe user-facing message is the same for all three, and the real error is hidden by `NewSilentError`. I reproduced scenario 3 directly:\n\n```\n$ ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=\"http://localhost:8787\" entire recap --static\nSign in with `entire login` to use `entire recap`.   # misleading!\n```\n\nThe actual error there is `base URL check: refusing to use insecure http://...` — re-running `entire login` won't help because you're already logged in. This perfectly matches your description: *\"users logged into entire and have it enabled, but they're told to re-run login first.\"*\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- This is a \"misleading error\" anti-pattern: a code path collapses three distinct failure modes into one user message, then drops the real error via `NewSilentError(err)` so the user never sees the actual cause. Compare with `dispatch_wizard.go:34` which just returns the underlying error.\n- `activity_cmd.go:61` has the exact same pattern (`\"Not logged in. Run 'entire login' to authenticate.\"` regardless of cause). `recap` and `activity` were almost certainly copy-pasted.\n- The TUI fetch path (`recap_errors.go:27`) gets this right — it inspects `*api.HTTPError` and produces a different message per status code. The pre-flight auth check is the laggard.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## What I'd suggest\n\nThe cleanest fix is to surface the wrapped error from `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient` (which is already informative) rather than always printing the same hint. Something like:\n- If the underlying error is \"not logged in\" → keep the \"Sign in with `entire login`\" hint.\n- Otherwise → print the actual error so the user can see it's a base-URL or keyring issue.\n\nWant me to make this fix in `recap.go` (and the matching one in `activity_cmd.go`)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_read_input_tokens":98060,"output_tokens":1909,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1909,"cache_read_input_tokens":98060,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caqkx9XhYHzK24uQYWT4D","type":"assistant","uuid":"c9bc1bb7-d8ae-48d0-9226-c297a2f33891","timestamp":"2026-05-08T20:48:27.261Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2","sessionId":"f24e472c-1007-4285-9f59-c6ba99a88a0f","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"review-fix-2"}
