{"parentUuid":"e3acc217-b5a1-45c8-8d14-9008bc9c2fa6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0155SACqaRCsCt4dGPoSRNw1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Same root cause — I just didn't connect the dots clearly enough. All three symptoms are *one* bug.\n\nLook at `recap.go:112-145` again:\n\n```go\nfunc runRecap(ctx context.Context, w, errW io.Writer, f *recapFlags) error {\n    // ... git check, view check, color check ...\n    client, err := NewAuthenticatedAPIClient(f.insecureHTTP)\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintln(errW, \"Sign in with `entire login` to use `entire recap`.\")\n        return NewSilentError(err)              // ← EXITS HERE on first run\n    }\n    // ↓ never reached if auth fails ↓\n    rangeKey := f.rangeKey()                    // --week / --month / --90 used here\n    repoSlug := currentRepoSlug(ctx)\n    if f.useTUI(...) {\n        return runRecapTUI(ctx, client, ...)    // flag values consumed here\n    }\n    resp, err := recap.FetchMeRecap(...)        // data fetched here\n    fmt.Fprint(w, recap.RenderStaticRecap(...)) // data rendered here\n}\n```\n\nCobra parses every flag into `f` *before* `runRecap` runs — so `--week`, `--static`, `--agent` all parse fine. But the auth check is **above** every line that actually *uses* those flags or fetches data. When auth fails, the function returns at line 128 and:\n\n- **No data shows** → because `FetchMeRecap` (line 142) is never called.\n- **Flags \"don't work\"** → because every code path that consumes `f.week`, `f.month`, `f.agent`, etc. is below line 128. The flags are parsed but never reach the renderer or the API call. From the user's perspective, `--week` and `--month` look identical because both produce the same \"Sign in\" message.\n- **\"Re-run login\"** → because that's the one error message printed for *any* `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient` failure.\n\n**Why login won't fix it for some users:** `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient` (`api_client.go:14-29`) fails in three ways, only one of which login fixes:\n1. Token missing → ✅ login fixes\n2. Keyring read error (locked, perms) → ❌ login won't run either, same keyring\n3. `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://...` without `--insecure-http-auth` → ❌ token is fine, URL is the problem\n\nSo a user who's already logged in but hits case 2 or 3 sees the exact same \"no data + flags ignored + re-login\" experience as a brand-new user who genuinely needs to login. The single misleading message + the swallowed real error (`NewSilentError(err)` hides it) is what makes both look identical.\n\nAlso worth noting: `entire enable` does **not** call `entire login`. They're independent. A user who runs `entire enable` and reasonably assumes they're \"set up\" will hit the same wall on first `entire recap` because they never actually authenticated.\n\nWant me to fix `recap.go` so the real reason surfaces (and ideally also a one-time \"you need to run `entire login` after `entire enable`\" hint somewhere in the onboarding)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1361,"cache_read_input_tokens":104871,"output_tokens":1625,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1361,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1625,"cache_read_input_tokens":104871,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1361},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqmWNZv5gdtBzUJ8i6WC","type":"assistant","uuid":"6b5a6f1d-f498-4bdb-952d-52e112f82fbd","timestamp":"2026-05-08T20:55:42.540Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2","sessionId":"f24e472c-1007-4285-9f59-c6ba99a88a0f","version":"2.1