{"parentUuid":"8a802eb3-6d7f-4c65-a9ac-507187acfc65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015CgrFaJ4NBKBC5U48c3uwW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Summary of what changed in `cmd/entire/cli/recap.go`:\n\n**Before:** `runRecap` called `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient`, which fails hard on missing token / locked keyring / insecure URL — and printed one fixed message (\"Sign in with `entire login`\") regardless. Flags below that line were never reached.\n\n**After:** New helper `newRecapClient` that:\n- Looks up the keyring token but **doesn't fail** when it's missing (passes empty string through to `api.NewClient`).\n- Only enforces the secure-URL check **when a token is present** — if there's no bearer to leak over HTTP, no need to refuse the call.\n- On a real misconfiguration (token + HTTP URL without `--insecure-http-auth`), returns the actual error instead of the misleading \"sign in\" hint.\n\nThe fetch path (`FetchMeRecap` → `handleRecapFetchError` → `recapLoadErrorMessage`) already mapped 401 to *\"Run `entire login` to re-authenticate.\"*, 404 to *\"could not find your account\"*, etc. — so we just stopped short-circuiting around that and let it do its job.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Verified flags now reach the API call by inspecting `since=` query params for `--day` (`2026-05-08`), `--week` (`2026-05-02`), `--month` (`2026-05-01`), `--90` (`2026-02-08`) — each one materially different. Before the fix all four produced the same \"Sign in\" message and never built a URL at all.\n- The `RequireSecureURL` check is now scoped to \"we have a bearer token to leak\" rather than being a blanket gate. This is a small semantic improvement: a brand-new user pointed at an HTTP dev endpoint can still see what the recap looks like (a 401 from the dev server) instead of being blocked by a check that protects against leaking a token they don't have.\n- Test scenarios: `mise run lint` clean, full `cmd/entire/cli` test suite passes (38s), and all four manual scenarios (logged-in, fake-host, HTTP-no-flag, HTTP-with-flag) produce distinct, accurate messages instead of one collapsed \"sign in\" hint.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1655,"cache_read_input_tokens":130029,"output_tokens":768,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1655,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":768,"cache_read_input_tokens":130029,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1655},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqnFFGpS9Uy3xueSwCSN","type":"assistant","uuid":"5be4c7c0-5217-47fa-9add-28de535ec19b","timestamp":"2026-05-08T21:05:13.889Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2","sessionId":"f24e472c-1007-4285-9f59-c6ba99a88a0f","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"review-fix-2"}
