ng a fixed status is enough to exercise the full client→server→error-mapping pipeline. This pattern would also work as an automated integration test if we wanted to lock in the behavior — `httptest.NewServer` in Go is the same idea.\n- Notice that the 401 message is *different* from the BEFORE message (\"Sign in with `entire login` to use `entire recap`.\" vs \"Run `entire login` to re-authenticate.\"). That's not just cosmetic: the new message is produced by the response-level error mapper that already existed in `recap_errors.go:27-28` for users whose tokens *expired*. The fix didn't add a new \"no token\" code path — it just stopped short-circuiting around the existing one, so genuine 401s and expired-token 401s now share the same well-tested message.\n- For the genuine logged-out walk-through (`entire logout && entire recap && entire login`), you'd see the same \"Run `entire login` to re-authenticate.\" message coming back from the real entire.io server — same code path as the mock above.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2066,"cache_read_input_tokens":154872,"output_tokens":1519,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2066,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1519,"cache_read_input_tokens":154872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2066},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqozaACHY3wP59jBvWh8","type":"assistant","uuid":"058f2633-5f63-47f2-a36d-2cfb7b870447","timestamp":"2026-05-08T21:28:18.666Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2","sessionId":"f24e472c-1007-4285-9f59-c6ba